+# Stub Division jurisdiction classification implementation plan
+
+## Scope
+
+Implement the design in
+`2026-08-02-stub-division-jurisdiction-classification-design.md`.
+
+## Tasks
+
+1. Add a private `GeneratePipeline` helper for Jurisdiction generation.
+2. Reuse the helper from the existing successful-match path without changing
+   its LSAD input.
+3. Invoke the helper from the no-validation-match path with no LSAD value.
+4. Preserve quarantine data and the `partial` response status.
+5. Add unit tests mirroring `src/init_migration/generate_pipeline.py`.
+
+## Test cases
+
+### No validation match
+
+- a stub Division is written;
+- classification is still invoked;
+- the classifier receives `lsad_code=None`;
+- quarantine reason remains `no_validation_match`; and
+- response status remains `partial`.
+
+### Reusable OCD ID classification
+
+- a county stub can produce a `government` Jurisdiction;
+- the generated Jurisdiction path is returned; and
+- the jurisdiction OCD ID is added to the existing deduplication set.
+
+## Validation
+
+Run:
+
+```bash
+uv run pytest tests/src/init_migration/test_generate_pipeline_stub_classification.py
+uv run ruff check src/init_migration/generate_pipeline.py tests/src/init_migration/test_generate_pipeline_stub_classification.py
+```
